WEBVTT

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:56.330
Are we saved?

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:58.330
Somewhat.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:01:59.910
Now, let's go.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:07.670
Hannah?

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.300
Hey, get up, Hannah.

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:15.230
Hannah...

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:34.130
You are...

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:41.920
No...

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:44.540
Hey, Papa.

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:48.640
May I download a new bag?

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:49.560
Okay.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.430
All right!

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:51.240
Let's see...

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:55.770
This one.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.930
I don't really know, so...

00:03:58.930 --> 00:03:59.410
Thank you.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:02.780
All right!

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:06.780
I was in 2.0 when I was young.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.310
The digital world and the real world were separate.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:12.010
A reality you can't play with is no fun.

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:14.540
Put your clothes on properly before you go.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:15.630
It's only good manners.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:16.710
Okay.

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:18.790
It's okay to enjoy the party,

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:20.520
but don't download illegal things.

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:22.260
Understand, Mishio?

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:24.080
I know.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.260
I'm not that stupid.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:28.470
Also, at least wear clothes inside the house—

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:29.520
Okay, okay.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:50.660
Here it is.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.220
Do you mind if I borrow this for a while, Grandma?

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:04.600
This is old!

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:08.820
Father's old embarrassing memories?

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.610
"We have a case, Watson-kun."

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:21.880
He truly was a ruffian when he was a kid.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:25.680
The CEO of the Maeno Group Holdings did this?

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:29.580
Rin?

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:31.520
This is old!

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:32.470
Rin-san.

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.090
What are you recording?

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:36.290
Who is this?

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:38.580
Could she be father's old girlfriend?

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:41.490
Oh no, it's already time.

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:06.830
Ah, it's that rumor?

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.160
Immortals or something, Fruits of Time?

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:13.860
Young people sure think about strange things.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:19.180
Well then, please convey my regards to your father.

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:20.080
Yes.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:20.780
Later.

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:25.080
You look bored.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:26.780
There aren't any nice guys.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:27.880
What about me?

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:28.610
Out of the question.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.140
You actually said it.

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:32.280
I'm popular elsewhere, you know.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:34.800
Then you should go elsewhere.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.470
It has nothing to do with me.

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:40.450
Do they exist somewhere?

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:44.330
Nice guys who would give tens of billions just like that to go out with me.

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:46.940
It would be a joke if someone else said it,

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:49.580
but you sound serious when you say it.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:53.080
Say, who is that?

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.330
The red, flashy one.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:57.500
Mrs. Numata from Yotsubishi.

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.520
No, the one to the right of her.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.590
The beautiful woman wearing a black dress.

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:06.490
I think she's with James & Will.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:07.540
Should I look in the register?

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:09.350
It's okay. You don't have to go that far.

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:11.280
Is something wrong with her?

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:13.860
Just a bit.

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:16.510
I'm pretty sure

00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:17.560
that she's named Rin.

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:22.360
You like the Impressionists.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:27.120
Is it because politics is all about the concrete?

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:33.570
What do you want, boy?

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:36.380
You mustn't judge people by their appearances.

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:39.890
I'm going to tell you something interesting.

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:46.470
Anji-sama.

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:50.380
Numata-sama from Yotsubishi would like to meet you.

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:55.690
Also, Mrs. Claudel from James & Will wants you to contact her.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:37.850
Very well.

00:08:38.390 --> 00:08:40.010
Thank you.

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:42.270
Also, the project plans from earlier

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:43.790
were very well done.

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:44.820
Really?

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:48.930
But I can't let you get involved with the project itself.

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:52.830
I'll probably take control of it myself.

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:56.680
Very well.

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:21.010
It is said that Yaobikuni gained immortality by eating mermaids.

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:24.820
Whether it's east or west,
people have always yearned for immortality.

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:31.830
Also, Emperor Qin Shi Huang ordered a sorcerer named
Xu Fu to obtain medicines for immortality from Penglai Island.

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:35.970
Penglai Island was said to be Japan.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:45.090
In Japan, the Emperor ordered a certain man to find a medicine for immortality called the Fruit from the Fragrant Tree of Time.

00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:47.040
His name was Tajimamori.

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:54.060
Unfortunately, by the time he found that medicine,
the Emperor was already dead.

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.360
Rin.

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:00.510
Maeno.

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:00.870
Yes.

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:06.920
After that, Tajimamori's clan was said to have split into Tajima, Kuki, and Maeno.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:09.120
Are there any legends in your household?

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:11.770
None at all.

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:14.070
That's too bad.

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:18.370
If there really was a Fruit from the Fragrant Tree of Time,
I'd like to have a few.

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:22.110
Now then, if we turn to India,

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:24.990
there is a scripture called the Rig Veda in Brahmanism,

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:29.090
in which the King of the Land of Gold rises up and...

00:10:29.090 --> 00:10:31.010
What is it?

00:10:31.010 --> 00:10:32.290
I'm in the middle of a class.

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:34.500
It's just a folklore class, right?

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.280
That's easy.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:37.850
Never mind that. Let's go play.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:39.860
Sounds great. I'm on my way.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:48.070
You are...

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:50.900
Is that right?

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:53.830
You want the project that much?

00:10:57.850 --> 00:10:59.830
Are you really sure you don't want me to take you home?

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:03.100
I'm Maeno Mishio! I'm okay!

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:04.910
You're not okay.

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:06.860
Shut up. Go home.

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:08.970
Then, I'm going back.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:10.270
Later.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:15.350
I'm going home.

00:11:18.890 --> 00:11:19.690
I'm sorry.

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:24.160
Rin?

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:37.440
Hey.

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:39.140
Hello?

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:41.460
Are you all right?

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:43.960
You're going to catch a cold.

00:11:57.840 --> 00:11:58.790
Hey, you.

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:02.260
Did you install an illegal program or something?

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:04.190
There's no corpse.

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:10.720
Maeno Mishio.

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:13.140
Excuse me!

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:14.440
What's wrong?

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:17.450
You fool, she's the daughter of the Maeno Group's CEO!

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:20.200
Our sponsor?

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:26.330
She really was there!

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:28.080
She really was dead!

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:34.060
A disappearing corpse.

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:37.180
A mysterious woman who left the scene.

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:41.570
Moreover, she might be related to some girl's father.

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:44.350
"Isn't this a real case, Watson-kun?"

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:48.670
"But Holmes, this is data from many decades ago."

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:51.520
"Are you sure you weren't seeing someone else?"

00:12:52.090 --> 00:12:53.680
"Think about it logically."

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:58.980
"Once you eliminate the impossible, whatever remains,
however improbable, must be the truth."

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:01.830
"We should start with the register from the recent party."

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:07.830
Saito Tamaki from James & Will.

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:09.940
Not Rin?

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:12.890
But these two...

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:14.370
Are they unrelated?

00:13:18.090 --> 00:13:18.830
What is that?

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:20.130
Didn't you see it?

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:22.010
You know, the thing that lets you become immortal.

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:23.270
The Fruit of Time?

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:23.850
Is it a fruit?

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:25.340
Not that.

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:26.600
The Yggdrasill thing?

00:13:27.190 --> 00:13:28.210
That's just a rumor.

00:13:28.210 --> 00:13:29.910
Something like that couldn't possibly exist.

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:31.840
Hey, hey, have you heard?

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:33.830
Chief Claudel from the development group, right?

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.110
She's missing.

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:38.260
That's right. She was your boss, wasn't she?

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:39.750
Know any likely places?

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:42.500
No. But she was a terrible person.

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:51.130
We can't contact Mrs. Claudel anymore.

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:02.650
Tamaki, see you later.

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:03.400
See you later.

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:21.780
Hi.

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:24.410
Hey, can we meet for a bit?

00:14:24.410 --> 00:14:25.800
I can't.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:26.790
What if you download it?

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:31.290
A physical program... You know that doesn't work too well, right?

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:32.960
That's right.

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:37.700
Then can we have dinner or something?

00:14:37.700 --> 00:14:39.180
Yeah.

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:42.180
Cheers.

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:51.280
It's obvious that you're watching them.

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:53.560
This duck is delicious.

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:56.060
Hey, do you know the guy she's sitting with?

00:14:56.470 --> 00:14:57.750
I don't.

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:59.240
Look him up!

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:00.100
No way I can do that!

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:01.860
It's private information!

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:04.400
I'm just playing along with your detective game.

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:05.340
It's not a game!

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:06.590
I got it.

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:08.080
Don't shout.

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:12.570
Tamaki.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:15.420
Have you thought about that?

00:15:20.960 --> 00:15:23.460
You're a nice guy...

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:24.360
Tamaki.

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:32.630
You...

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:35.510
don't know about me.

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:37.150
Neither do I.

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:38.810
Tamaki.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:42.290
If that's even my real name.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:44.330
But, that's...

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:45.600
I...

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:48.370
don't have any memories of the past.

00:15:49.570 --> 00:15:51.120
Where I was born...

00:15:51.650 --> 00:15:52.670
Not even my real name.

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:54.590
I don't know at all.

00:15:57.800 --> 00:15:59.630
Five years ago,

00:16:00.010 --> 00:16:01.970
I washed up on a seashore.

00:16:01.970 --> 00:16:03.390
I'd been saved.

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:14.900
This was what I had in my hands at the time.

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:28.120
I'm sorry.

00:16:30.370 --> 00:16:31.770
Hey, look at that.

00:16:32.270 --> 00:16:33.050
What is it?

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:34.550
That, that.

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:39.200
Hey, she was crying.

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:40.770
Maybe they were talking about breaking up?

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:41.390
I wonder?

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:45.680
Follow her, you ladykiller.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:47.850
Mishio?

00:17:09.650 --> 00:17:10.500
Yes.

00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:17.430
Again?

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:20.600
You never say anything.

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:23.630
But it's okay.

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:25.330
I...

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:27.330
I...

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:42.640
Welcome back.

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:43.660
Yes.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:44.500
Hey.

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:45.210
What is it?

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:46.860
A digital dress again?

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:48.640
Who is Rin?

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.340
Where did you find this data?

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:53.960
It was on Grandma's shelf.

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:55.840
I see.

00:17:57.200 --> 00:17:58.040
Who is she?

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:01.620
Asougi Rin-san.

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:04.560
She saved my life.

00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:08.050
Thanks to her, I can be the way I am now.

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:09.550
Was she your lover?

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:11.560
No. That's not it.

00:18:12.670 --> 00:18:13.530
Damn.

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.930
Then she's not your long-lost sister either?

00:18:16.260 --> 00:18:17.930
What are you saying?

00:18:17.930 --> 00:18:20.660
She's probably Rin's daughter,

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:21.940
but I met someone who looks just like her.

00:18:22.590 --> 00:18:25.500
And then, when I went drinking with Tajima recently...

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:26.510
Where?

00:18:26.510 --> 00:18:27.610
Where did you meet her?

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:49.770
That's...

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:51.090
Anji-sama.

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:17.270
Rin-san.

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:19.080
Rin-san!

00:19:22.310 --> 00:19:23.890
Just as I expected.

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:25.090
You're alive.

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:27.720
It's me, Maeno Teruki.

00:19:29.610 --> 00:19:32.430
Is it possible that you know about my past?

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:36.750
I don't remember the past.

00:19:36.750 --> 00:19:37.760
Please.

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:39.560
What kind of person was I?

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:41.520
Please, tell me.

00:19:46.810 --> 00:19:47.860
I'm sorry.

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:50.770
It seems I have the wrong person.

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:53.960
Wait!

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:54.810
Please!

00:19:55.310 --> 00:19:56.210
Wait!

00:19:57.580 --> 00:19:58.410
Please!

00:20:03.850 --> 00:20:06.250
Who is... Rin?

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:08.290
I don't know.

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:10.350
Help me.

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:13.550
Ihika.

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:21.880
It's a beautiful garden.

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:26.280
So you think this lonely garden is beautiful?

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:28.150
You're getting old.

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:32.460
I'm so old that I even think you look good as a nun.

00:20:37.100 --> 00:20:39.010
You managed to find this place.

00:20:39.010 --> 00:20:41.610
I asked Numata-kun from Yotsubishi.

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:44.180
I heard Mrs. Numata is studying with you?

00:20:44.180 --> 00:20:49.060
Now you're even able to order Yotsubishi around.

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:51.130
Many things have happened since then.

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:53.620
The world moved on.

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:55.420
I kept on running.

00:20:55.860 --> 00:20:59.650
And when I looked back,
I'd become the leader of some corporate group.

00:21:01.830 --> 00:21:05.650
From Numata-kun, I heard about this nun in Kyoto that lives forever.

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:08.690
They call you Imayobikuni, I heard?

00:21:08.690 --> 00:21:10.640
Many things have happened to me, actually.

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:15.480
Before I noticed, I'd become a nun that talks about prophecies.

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:26.400
Rin-san is alive.

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:27.920
I met her too.

00:21:28.650 --> 00:21:31.180
Rin's eyes were the eyes of the people who want to kill me.

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:32.380
That can't be!

00:21:37.130 --> 00:21:38.890
She is hunting the immortals.

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:44.140
My daughter said Rin-san is involved with some murder.

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:48.270
If we think about the time frame,

00:21:48.270 --> 00:21:49.470
that would be Lona Claudel.

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:51.160
She was an immortal?

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:56.520
We rarely fail to notice others like us.

00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:59.740
Even if we're together for a long time,
sometimes we don't know.

00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:01.830
After Rin disappeared,

00:22:01.830 --> 00:22:05.040
I tried to build a network of acquaintances.

00:22:05.040 --> 00:22:07.960
But recently, the number of people I can't contact has been increasing.

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:10.850
You're saying that Rin-san is responsible?

00:22:10.850 --> 00:22:11.700
No way.

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:13.960
She lost her memory.

00:22:14.480 --> 00:22:16.630
Or maybe Apos is controlling her?

00:22:17.180 --> 00:22:20.970
In the first place, can we ever really lose our memories?

00:22:21.390 --> 00:22:22.440
Apos?

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:25.480
But did you really see Rin-san?

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:15.500
That hurts.

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:16.470
Why?

00:23:16.470 --> 00:23:18.500
It's Christmas Eve. Why is it you?

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:20.670
Why isn't it some nice guy?

00:23:21.590 --> 00:23:22.980
Maybe because it's fate?

00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:24.670
There's no way something like that would happen!

00:23:26.360 --> 00:23:27.340
I'm sorry—

00:23:30.060 --> 00:23:31.340
What are you doing?

00:23:32.380 --> 00:23:33.680
What's wrong, Mishio?

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:35.030
Come, Watson-kun.

00:23:35.450 --> 00:23:36.380
Hey, wait!

00:23:43.780 --> 00:23:44.390
No.

00:23:54.530 --> 00:23:55.610
No.

00:23:56.100 --> 00:23:57.700
At least take a shower first.

00:24:19.120 --> 00:24:21.220
Merry Christmas!

00:24:39.700 --> 00:24:40.800
Ihika?

00:24:42.910 --> 00:24:43.820
Ihika?

00:24:47.160 --> 00:24:49.580
A present for good children!

00:24:59.450 --> 00:25:00.700
Wh-What's happening?

00:25:01.130 --> 00:25:02.290
Th-The police.

00:25:02.290 --> 00:25:03.440
I called them already.

00:25:04.410 --> 00:25:05.590
Hey, that's illegal.

00:25:06.120 --> 00:25:07.600
I can't let them die.

00:25:08.010 --> 00:25:09.810
What? Why?

00:25:10.330 --> 00:25:11.980
The same face?

00:25:12.420 --> 00:25:15.400
Because there's someone who called me Rin.

00:25:15.400 --> 00:25:17.600
That's how I knew you were alive.

00:25:21.370 --> 00:25:22.390
It hurts!

00:25:23.070 --> 00:25:23.890
It hurts!

00:25:23.890 --> 00:25:27.330
You seem to have lost your memory.

00:25:27.330 --> 00:25:29.120
Apparently it's real.

00:25:29.120 --> 00:25:30.860
Help me! Ihika!

00:25:34.660 --> 00:25:37.510
Apos must be disappointed with this.

00:25:46.170 --> 00:25:47.220
A Fruit of Time?

00:25:47.770 --> 00:25:48.570
Why?

00:25:49.250 --> 00:25:50.370
Well, doesn't matter.

00:25:50.370 --> 00:25:51.770
I'll take this back too.

00:25:54.290 --> 00:25:55.340
There are two Tamaki?

00:25:55.340 --> 00:25:55.900
Why?

00:26:04.040 --> 00:26:04.970
Ow...

00:26:08.310 --> 00:26:09.490
Hey, are you okay?

00:26:09.880 --> 00:26:11.080
Somehow.

00:26:11.570 --> 00:26:15.250
If I don't train my body, a physical program doesn't work.

00:26:15.700 --> 00:26:20.750
Still, you broke through the door with perfect timing, Watson-kun.

00:26:20.750 --> 00:26:23.660
You know, you have to stop this.

00:26:23.660 --> 00:26:25.730
You might be the one that gets hit first.

00:26:25.730 --> 00:26:29.140
Humans react to things that move.

00:26:29.140 --> 00:26:29.970
Even if they don't want to.

00:26:30.390 --> 00:26:31.500
Geez.

00:26:31.500 --> 00:26:32.440
Can you walk?

00:26:32.440 --> 00:26:33.460
No.

00:26:33.460 --> 00:26:35.410
My ankle is broken... probably.

00:26:36.170 --> 00:26:36.690
Also...

00:26:37.370 --> 00:26:39.420
Three partitions is rough.

00:26:42.280 --> 00:26:45.380
Both the killer and victim are Saito Tamaki?

00:26:54.960 --> 00:26:56.710
They're both real.

00:26:59.440 --> 00:27:01.500
Damn you.

00:27:08.210 --> 00:27:09.090
You.

00:27:18.430 --> 00:27:19.130
Run!

00:27:23.040 --> 00:27:26.700
I heard earnings from the microwave department are deteriorating.

00:27:26.700 --> 00:27:30.580
Illegal transmissions from data carriers are increasing,
and that works against us.

00:27:31.030 --> 00:27:31.930
Is that right?

00:27:32.880 --> 00:27:35.470
Is James from MPA here?

00:27:35.470 --> 00:27:36.070
Yes.

00:27:36.070 --> 00:27:37.620
He's been waiting for a while.

00:27:38.140 --> 00:27:40.280
Let him wait a bit longer.

00:27:40.280 --> 00:27:44.230
He seems to have grown enough to read our expressions.

00:27:45.080 --> 00:27:49.100
What about your dinner with Ananda Hermanda?

00:27:49.660 --> 00:27:53.710
To deal with a combination of the three great merchant companies in the world...

00:27:55.030 --> 00:27:55.860
What's wrong, Mishio?

00:27:56.710 --> 00:27:57.510
Teruki?

00:27:59.910 --> 00:28:00.860
Rin-san.

00:28:01.380 --> 00:28:02.690
I wanted to meet you.

00:28:04.770 --> 00:28:06.820
I don't remember inviting you.

00:28:08.040 --> 00:28:12.950
Or has the situation reached a point that requires meeting me?

00:28:20.470 --> 00:28:22.460
Shut up, old man.

00:28:23.490 --> 00:28:25.960
Is this my reward for having wasted time?

00:28:26.590 --> 00:28:29.090
I'm not the one who doesn't have time.

00:28:29.820 --> 00:28:31.180
It's Yggdrasill.

00:28:31.710 --> 00:28:32.630
Really?

00:28:36.240 --> 00:28:39.560
It can kill even you.

00:28:40.050 --> 00:28:41.380
Fool.

00:28:41.380 --> 00:28:43.660
You're the fool.

00:28:43.660 --> 00:28:45.440
Regarding Rin as well.

00:28:46.050 --> 00:28:47.580
Damn you.

00:28:48.220 --> 00:28:50.320
I'm going to take her.

00:28:51.140 --> 00:28:54.330
You can stay here and eat Fruits of Time,

00:28:54.330 --> 00:28:58.000
and live your miserable life forever.

00:28:58.000 --> 00:28:59.510
You, the former god.

00:29:02.900 --> 00:29:04.180
Rin.

00:29:18.630 --> 00:29:19.530
So then?

00:29:29.720 --> 00:29:31.830
Mishio-chan, was it?

00:29:32.510 --> 00:29:33.560
How's your daughter?

00:29:33.560 --> 00:29:34.660
She's fine.

00:29:34.660 --> 00:29:36.390
She's resting in her room.

00:29:36.390 --> 00:29:38.350
I got her in trouble.

00:29:38.350 --> 00:29:40.370
She's a reckless girl.

00:29:41.190 --> 00:29:43.090
But she saved me.

00:29:43.940 --> 00:29:45.090
Is her ankle okay?

00:29:45.700 --> 00:29:47.610
Just a simple fracture.

00:29:47.610 --> 00:29:48.960
It will heal soon.

00:29:51.340 --> 00:29:53.190
Did you get your memories back?

00:29:54.430 --> 00:29:55.100
Yes.

00:29:55.710 --> 00:30:00.640
That was the first time my body was completely destroyed.

00:30:05.170 --> 00:30:08.270
Reconstructing my body probably took decades,

00:30:08.270 --> 00:30:10.400
and my memory ended up in chaos.

00:30:10.400 --> 00:30:12.060
Because of that...

00:30:12.060 --> 00:30:13.820
I needed a restart.

00:30:17.840 --> 00:30:21.830
Before, you left me because you knew I had lost my memory, right?

00:30:23.510 --> 00:30:24.460
Thank you.

00:30:24.460 --> 00:30:25.300
No.

00:30:25.970 --> 00:30:28.030
You're kind, Teruki.

00:30:28.030 --> 00:30:29.230
It was cruel, though.

00:30:30.490 --> 00:30:34.070
If you're dreaming, there are times when you don't want to wake up, right?

00:30:34.070 --> 00:30:35.120
That's right.

00:30:36.010 --> 00:30:38.810
It's been many centuries since I had a lover.

00:30:39.670 --> 00:30:41.220
It was a sweet dream.

00:30:49.800 --> 00:30:51.600
It was a dream. This too.

00:30:53.320 --> 00:30:53.890
Good night.

00:30:59.770 --> 00:31:01.830
Who are you?

00:31:02.960 --> 00:31:06.110
Why... do I have this?

00:31:22.880 --> 00:31:23.830
Ihika...

00:31:26.680 --> 00:31:28.390
Failure?

00:31:35.390 --> 00:31:36.370
I have a present.

00:31:37.000 --> 00:31:38.900
A present?

00:31:44.100 --> 00:31:47.340
Well, only your looks are similar.

00:31:48.450 --> 00:31:51.700
Even though I took the trouble to move many things.

00:31:56.200 --> 00:32:00.350
You don't know how important Rin is.

00:32:14.810 --> 00:32:15.940
Rin.

00:32:51.160 --> 00:32:52.380
Now then.

00:32:52.380 --> 00:32:52.690
Hey.

00:32:53.230 --> 00:32:54.130
What is it?

00:32:54.130 --> 00:32:56.310
Tell me about your past.

00:32:56.310 --> 00:32:58.190
That's all right, but how much?

00:32:59.640 --> 00:33:01.190
Let's see...

00:33:11.190 --> 00:33:12.160
Rin is coming.

00:33:12.520 --> 00:33:15.630
Rin is not the one who owns us.

00:33:16.130 --> 00:33:18.220
That's what Maeno said.

00:33:18.220 --> 00:33:19.460
Maeno?

00:33:19.460 --> 00:33:20.700
Yes.

00:33:20.700 --> 00:33:22.670
Mimi, do you believe it?

00:33:22.670 --> 00:33:24.070
I want to believe it.

00:33:24.520 --> 00:33:29.470
But from what we've seen,
we know very well what's going on behind the scenes.

00:33:29.960 --> 00:33:31.650
You know the rumors on the net?

00:33:32.090 --> 00:33:33.690
About Fruits of Time, right?

00:33:34.210 --> 00:33:36.780
The rumors surfaced about a month ago.

00:33:36.780 --> 00:33:39.300
The information is relatively correct.

00:33:39.300 --> 00:33:41.470
But the idea that you become immortal if you eat it

00:33:41.470 --> 00:33:42.640
is a fantasy.

00:33:42.640 --> 00:33:45.640
Is one of our comrades leaking information?

00:33:45.640 --> 00:33:47.430
It might be Apos.

00:33:47.430 --> 00:33:48.940
No way.

00:33:48.940 --> 00:33:53.640
Because the ones who are saying this can't see Yggdrasill.

00:33:53.640 --> 00:33:56.420
Have you seen Yggdrasill since Rin disappeared?

00:33:57.400 --> 00:34:01.260
Nobody knows when Yggdrasill will appear.

00:34:01.260 --> 00:34:03.450
Sometimes we see it after a few months,

00:34:03.450 --> 00:34:05.250
sometimes we don't see it for a few years.

00:34:05.800 --> 00:34:07.430
But it's been thirty years.

00:34:07.430 --> 00:34:09.370
Has something happened to Yggdrasill?

00:34:09.370 --> 00:34:10.170
Probably.

00:34:10.760 --> 00:34:12.650
It's trying to change something.

00:34:13.910 --> 00:34:16.390
Apos should know as well.

00:34:44.910 --> 00:34:46.710
You're so shallow.

00:34:47.230 --> 00:34:49.850
Do you really want these that badly?

00:34:52.350 --> 00:34:53.850
You're indecent.

00:35:10.660 --> 00:35:14.310
You too will become a Seraphim's Egg eventually.

00:35:45.030 --> 00:35:47.330
It's been a long time since I last visited Kyoto.

00:35:48.100 --> 00:35:48.850
Mishio-chan?

00:35:50.170 --> 00:35:51.090
I came by linear rail.

00:35:51.090 --> 00:35:53.590
My sense of history...

00:35:53.590 --> 00:35:55.540
You're the one who asked me to tell you.

00:35:55.540 --> 00:35:59.390
But Nobunaga isn't...!

00:35:59.390 --> 00:36:01.240
That's just my subjective view.

00:36:01.240 --> 00:36:02.540
But...

00:36:10.090 --> 00:36:11.300
Rin!

00:36:15.700 --> 00:36:16.500
Genta.

00:36:17.080 --> 00:36:17.880
Look.

00:36:18.370 --> 00:36:19.170
It's Rin.

00:36:36.340 --> 00:36:38.800
You won't die from just this, right?

00:36:38.800 --> 00:36:40.120
Since you're a cyborg.

00:36:40.510 --> 00:36:42.620
Even though your hands are stained red with blood,

00:36:43.150 --> 00:36:45.630
your blood seems black as night.

00:36:45.630 --> 00:36:48.080
And it's colder than darkness.

00:36:48.080 --> 00:36:49.850
The same as dead people.

00:36:49.850 --> 00:36:52.670
It's okay. I won't kill you yet.

00:36:52.670 --> 00:36:55.170
There are lots of things I want to ask you.

00:36:57.980 --> 00:36:59.800
What's so funny?

00:36:59.800 --> 00:37:02.550
Because I knew all of you were gathering here.

00:37:03.050 --> 00:37:05.870
Do you think I came here without making plans?

00:37:05.870 --> 00:37:06.670
What?

00:37:09.430 --> 00:37:10.680
Th-This is...

00:37:11.200 --> 00:37:12.070
Anji-sama...

00:37:14.720 --> 00:37:15.570
No...

00:37:20.390 --> 00:37:21.390
Now.

00:37:21.390 --> 00:37:23.640
Embrace them as much as you want.

00:37:26.710 --> 00:37:27.840
Rin...

00:37:41.520 --> 00:37:43.620
Stop drinking, Ivan.

00:37:45.210 --> 00:37:46.810
Try eating this.

00:37:48.130 --> 00:37:51.240
It will stop you from thinking you're near your end.

00:37:51.820 --> 00:37:54.990
In exchange for this, I need a favor from you.

00:37:59.740 --> 00:38:01.090
What?

00:38:02.240 --> 00:38:04.090
It's something simple.

00:38:07.510 --> 00:38:09.070
We're going to climb this?

00:38:09.070 --> 00:38:10.050
Why?

00:38:10.050 --> 00:38:12.750
Mimi-san's place isn't too far away, right?

00:38:14.380 --> 00:38:15.620
Wh-What's wrong?

00:38:15.620 --> 00:38:16.340
Are you not feeling well?

00:38:17.030 --> 00:38:19.280
Rin-san? Why?

00:38:26.710 --> 00:38:29.280
Do you have something to protect yourself with?

00:38:30.610 --> 00:38:33.710
Y-Yes, I have a stun gun from Dad.

00:38:37.600 --> 00:38:39.200
Don't move from here.

00:38:40.660 --> 00:38:41.360
Okay.

00:38:56.070 --> 00:38:57.020
Genta.

00:38:58.500 --> 00:38:59.300
Genta...

00:39:15.530 --> 00:39:17.530
Good! Eat me more!

00:39:18.410 --> 00:39:19.530
Nao.

00:39:20.340 --> 00:39:21.580
Alisa.

00:39:25.470 --> 00:39:26.580
Looking at how you are now,

00:39:26.580 --> 00:39:30.080
your memories must have come back.

00:39:30.080 --> 00:39:31.570
Geez.

00:39:31.570 --> 00:39:35.530
These people all stink, but it can't be helped.

00:39:35.530 --> 00:39:36.470
Eat me...

00:39:44.790 --> 00:39:46.850
You're like that too, aren't you?

00:39:47.550 --> 00:39:50.850
You can feel the angels all around your body.

00:39:55.450 --> 00:39:56.570
Embrace me.

00:40:30.270 --> 00:40:33.870
You're able to maintain your will. You're someone to admire.

00:40:34.390 --> 00:40:36.030
Let me help you.

00:40:36.610 --> 00:40:38.580
You want your will to be obvious, don't you?

00:40:39.930 --> 00:40:41.180
Go away!

00:40:42.710 --> 00:40:45.690
You wasted three Fruits of Time.

00:40:45.690 --> 00:40:46.490
Useless thing.

00:40:54.860 --> 00:40:57.660
I can't let my guard down against you after all.

00:41:03.880 --> 00:41:05.980
You're getting in my way!

00:41:25.270 --> 00:41:27.420
I've been with you for a long time.

00:41:27.920 --> 00:41:28.970
That's right.

00:41:30.360 --> 00:41:32.790
Despite being around this long,

00:41:32.790 --> 00:41:35.670
I'm always thinking about you.

00:41:36.360 --> 00:41:38.810
Wondering what you're doing now, and things like that.

00:41:39.560 --> 00:41:41.670
I didn't think about you at all.

00:41:41.670 --> 00:41:43.580
I'm so unlucky.

00:41:44.070 --> 00:41:47.180
But the more I'm rejected, the more exciting I find the love.

00:41:48.420 --> 00:41:50.910
So let me remind you of one thing...

00:41:50.910 --> 00:41:52.900
of someone who is here.

00:41:52.900 --> 00:41:53.440
Mimi.

00:42:03.290 --> 00:42:03.860
Mimi?

00:42:12.920 --> 00:42:13.620
Mimi!

00:42:14.500 --> 00:42:15.550
Don't look.

00:42:16.620 --> 00:42:17.870
Here you are.

00:42:18.750 --> 00:42:21.630
You're so late. I was just killing time.

00:42:25.350 --> 00:42:26.610
Apos?

00:42:26.610 --> 00:42:27.510
You...

00:42:28.000 --> 00:42:28.920
That's right.

00:42:29.550 --> 00:42:31.840
I am a man, and not a man.

00:42:31.840 --> 00:42:34.060
A woman, and not a woman.

00:42:34.480 --> 00:42:36.650
An immortal angel.

00:42:44.260 --> 00:42:47.860
Th-This... is...

00:42:47.860 --> 00:42:51.370
Do you know what immortal angels are called?

00:42:54.980 --> 00:42:57.380
They are called gods.

00:43:20.800 --> 00:43:21.500
Rin...
